  "proof": [
    "The two coprime squarefree quadratic branch polynomials define independent square classes; their compositum is a genus-one curve.",
    "Each cover has a correction-aware exact positive-definite rank-10 Shioda Gram. The nine source sections are deck-invariant and the new section has a nonzero anti-invariant of positive exact height.",
    "The two cover involutions independently isolate the two new section coefficients in any relation; the remaining nine source sections are independent.",
    "The auxiliary genus-one base has a rational nontorsion point, hence infinitely many rational points.",
    "The elliptic curve has nonconstant j-invariant. Silverman specialization is injective for all but finitely many rational points of a curve base, so infinitely many of those rational base points specialize the rank-11 subgroup injectively.",
    "Smooth specialization at the common rational split parameter has exact rational torsion C2; specialization injectivity proves the generic rational torsion is exactly C2."
  ],
  "specialized_curve_rank_claim": null,
  "specialization_reference": "Silverman, Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves, Theorem C.20.3",
  "reference": "https://arxiv.org/html/2608.25406v1"
